Content security gateways provide organizations with a centralized layer for inspecting web traffic, email, file transfers, and other data streams while enforcing security policies. Their combination of threat intelligence, sandboxing, encryption inspection, and data-loss prevention is becoming increasingly important as organizations manage sensitive information across cloud and distributed environments.

